.Dd September 3, 2026
.Dt VDOTS-DOCTOR 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vdots-doctor
.Nd static health check for the vdots install
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -json
.Op Fl -fix
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the "brew doctor" for vdots: it checks the Neovim runtime diagnostics
.Pf ( via Xr vdots-ctl 1 Ic check )
plus the read-aloud support surface \(em the
.Xr say 1
engine, the compiled Swift media-key helper, the SwiftBar remote shim, the
listen library directory, Google Drive sync, and which audio time-stretch
engine is available
.Pf ( Xr rubberband 1 , Xr ffmpeg 1 Ic atempo , No or none ) .
It exits
.Ic 0
when no failures are found and
.Ic 1
on any
.Ic [FAIL] .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "--json"
.It Fl -json
Emit a single JSON object
.Pf ( Ic status , checks , readaloud , runtime ) .
.It Fl -fix
Build the media-key helper from
.Pa bin/vdots-mediakey-helper.swift ,
install the SwiftBar shim to
.Pa ~/.swiftbar/vdots-readaloud.5s.sh ,
and create the listen library directory.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr vdots 1 ,
.Xr vdots-ctl 1 ,
.Xr rubberband 1
.Pp
.Ic :checkhealth vdots.readaloud
inside Neovim.
